We note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *charge* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}$ is *inversely proportional to* the *time.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}∝\\frac{1}{t}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the number *decreases* with time, our derivative should be *negative*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{t}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143081" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6c2c5ea9b5746e6ed1772dac175dd03c8a7b8c460ec0c5f94330f3374a220fd0" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143081" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143081" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{C},\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143081" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{t},\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143081" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=-kC,\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143081" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{t},\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143081" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=kt,\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143081" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{t},\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143094" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The speed $S$ of an object decreases at a rate that's inversely proportional to the square of the travel time $t.$ What differential equation describes the rate of change of the speed $S?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143094" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **speed** $S$ of an object **decreases** at a rate that's **inversely proportional** to the **square of the travel time** $t.$*\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *speed* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}$ is *inversely proportional to* the *square of the travel time.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}∝\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the speed *decreases* with time, our derivative should be *negative*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{{t}^{2}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143094" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6c2c5ea9b5746e6ed1772dac175dd03c8a7b8c460ec0c5f94330f3374a220fd0" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143094" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143094" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{{S}^{2}},\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143094" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{{t}^{2}},\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143094" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=-k{t}^{2},\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143094" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{t},\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143094" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{{S}^{2}},\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The intensity $I$ of a light source with a motion sensor increases at a rate that's inversely proportional to the square of the distance $d$ from the source to the object detected by the sensor. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the intensity of the light source $I?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **intensity** $I$ of a light source with a motion sensor **increases** at a rate that's **inversely proportional** to the **square of the distance** $d$ from the source to the object detected by the sensor.*\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *intensity* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}I}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}I}{\\text{d}t}$ is *inversely proportional to* the *square of the distance.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}I}{\\text{d}t}∝\\frac{1}{{d}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the intensity *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}I}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{{d}^{2}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6c2c5ea9b5746e6ed1772dac175dd03c8a7b8c460ec0c5f94330f3374a220fd0" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143078" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143078" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}I}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{{d}^{2}},\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143078" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}I}{\\text{d}t}=-k{I}^{2},\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143078" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}I}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{{I}^{2}},\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143078" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}I}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{{d}^{2}},\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143078" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}I}{\\text{d}t}=k{d}^{2},\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-521" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A helium balloon loses $20$ grams of helium every second. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the mass $M$ of the balloon?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/example-521.json" "file_sha256" "82a94df7cd6e5ebc9808a806c2a21ab5425ff93fa9a46d8ecd654edca9f0c49f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-521" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If the mass of the balloon is $M$ grams, then the rate of change of the mass is $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}M}{\\textrm{d}t},$ where $t$ is the time in seconds.\n\nSince $20$ grams are lost every second, the rate of change of the balloon's mass is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}M}{\\textrm{d}t}=-20.\n$$\n\nNotice that the right-hand side is *negative* because the balloon is *losing* mass." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/example-521.json" "file_sha256" "82a94df7cd6e5ebc9808a806c2a21ab5425ff93fa9a46d8ecd654edca9f0c49f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-522" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The volume of water $V(t)$ in a leaking tank decreases at a rate that is proportional to the time $t$ (in minutes) since the leak started. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the volume of water at time $t?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/example-522.json" "file_sha256" "360fdfc935174ac42325438dbabd8e6e88395ea04267fab276787f744f0043af" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-522" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **volume** of water $V(t)$ in a leaking tank **decreases** at a **rate** that is **proportional** to the **time** $t$ (in minutes) since the leak started. *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *volume* of water varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d V}{\\textrm d t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\dfrac{\\textrm d V}{\\textrm d t}$ is *proportional to* the *time* since the water begins to leak.  In other words,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d V}{\\textrm d t} \\propto t.\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\propto$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the volume of water *decreases* with time, our derivative should be *negative*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d V}{\\textrm d t} = -kt.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/example-522.json" "file_sha256" "360fdfc935174ac42325438dbabd8e6e88395ea04267fab276787f744f0043af" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-10071" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The area $A$ of a forest decreases with time due to deforestation. The rate of change of the forest area is proportional to the square of the area. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the area at time $t?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/example-10071.json" "file_sha256" "a04d64a20c202c25e56ac95f36a0e9f8e8ed06845571e72b43627af8fb8f08fe" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-10071" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **area** $A$ of a forest **decreases** with time due to deforestation. The **rate** of change of the forest area is **proportional** to the **area squared**.  *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *area* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d A}{\\textrm d t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\dfrac{\\textrm d A}{\\textrm d t}$ is *proportional to* the *area squared.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d A}{\\textrm d t} \\propto A^2.\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\propto$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the area *decreases* with time, our derivative should be *negative*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d A}{\\textrm d t} = -kA^2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/example-10071.json" "file_sha256" "a04d64a20c202c25e56ac95f36a0e9f8e8ed06845571e72b43627af8fb8f08fe" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-10073" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The volume of water $V$ in a bucket decreases at a rate that's inversely proportional to the square of the volume of water. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the volume of water $V?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/example-10073.json" "file_sha256" "28ad930a4b2c8365a62358cfb07500640d3472f4ec035ebfbbd9f31b28443883" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-10073" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The  **volume of water** $V$  in a bucket **decreases** at a rate that's **inversely proportional** to the ** square of the volume of water** $V.$*\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *volume of water* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d V}{\\textrm d t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\dfrac{\\textrm d V}{\\textrm d t}$ is *inversely proportional to* the *square of the volume.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d V}{\\textrm d t} \\propto \\dfrac{1}{V^2}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\propto$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the volume of water *decreases* with time, our derivative should be *negative*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d V}{\\textrm d t} = -\\dfrac{k}{V^2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/example-10073.json" "file_sha256" "28ad930a4b2c8365a62358cfb07500640d3472f4ec035ebfbbd9f31b28443883" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-353456" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A bookstore sells $27$ copies of a particular novel every day. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the number of copies $N(t)$ remaining in stock? Assume that the time $t$ is measured in days.\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=$  \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-353456" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If the number of copies remaining in stock is $N,$ then the rate of change of the number of copies is $\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t},$ where $t$ is the time in days.\n\nSince $27$ copies are sold each day, the rate of change of the number of copies is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}N}{\\text{d}t}=-27.\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is negative because the number of copies remaining is *decreasing*." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-353456" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b08e89e3902ba9360f9961f50e9f3f1b8ba1a959fe0de04a87724d72ff237043"} {"question" "q-353456" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-353456" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-27"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-119052" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Tommy drinks $5$ milliliters of vitamin syrup each day from a bottle. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the amount of vitamin syrup $S$ (in milliliters) remaining in the bottle? Assume that the time $t$ is measured in days." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-119052" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If the amount of vitamin syrup remaining is $S$ milliliters, then the rate of change of the syrup volume is $\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t},$ where $t$ is the time in days.\n\nSince Tommy drinks $5$ milliliters of syrup each day, the rate of change of the amount of syrup remaining is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=-5.\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is negative because the amount of syrup is *decreasing*." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-119052" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b08e89e3902ba9360f9961f50e9f3f1b8ba1a959fe0de04a87724d72ff237043"} {"question" "q-119052" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-119052" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=-5"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=-5S"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=-5t"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=5"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{1}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-119052" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}=-5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-353449" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The number of completed online course enrollments increases by $18$ enrollments every hour during a promotional event. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the number of enrollments $E(t)?$ Assume that the time $t$ is measured in hours.\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}E}{\\text{d}t}=$  \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-353449" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If the number of enrollments is $E,$ then the rate of change of the number of enrollments is $\\frac{\\text{d}E}{\\text{d}t},$ where $t$ is the time in hours.\n\nSince $18$ new enrollments are added every hour, the rate of change of the number of enrollments is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}E}{\\text{d}t}=18.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-353449" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b08e89e3902ba9360f9961f50e9f3f1b8ba1a959fe0de04a87724d72ff237043"} {"question" "q-353449" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-353449" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "18"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-79304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A total of $2$ milliliters of water evaporate from a beaker every second.\nWhat differential equation describes the rate of change of the amount of water $W$ (in milliliters) remaining in the beaker?  Assume that the time $t$ is measured in seconds." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-79304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If the amount of water in the beaker is $W$ milliliters, then the rate of change of the amount of water is $\\frac{\\text{d}W}{\\text{d}t},$ where $t$ is the time in seconds.\n\nSince $2$ milliliters of water are lost every second, the rate of change of the amount of water is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}W}{\\text{d}t}=-2.\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is negative because the beaker is losing water." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-79304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b08e89e3902ba9360f9961f50e9f3f1b8ba1a959fe0de04a87724d72ff237043"} {"question" "q-79304" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-79304" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}W}{\\text{d}t}=-2"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}W}{\\text{d}t}=-2W"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}W}{\\text{d}t}=2"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}W}{\\text{d}t}=2Wt"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}W}{\\text{d}t}={e}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-79304" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}W}{\\text{d}t}=-2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-353450" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The distance traveled by a conveyor belt increases by $5$ meters every minute while it operates at a constant speed. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the distance traveled $X(t)?$ Assume that the time $t$ is measured in minutes.\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}X}{\\text{d}t}=$  \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-353450" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If the distance traveled is $X,$ then the rate of change of the distance traveled is $\\frac{\\text{d}X}{\\text{d}t},$ where $t$ is the time in minutes.\n\nSince the conveyor belt moves $5$ meters every minute, the rate of change of the distance traveled is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}X}{\\text{d}t}=5.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-353450" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b08e89e3902ba9360f9961f50e9f3f1b8ba1a959fe0de04a87724d72ff237043"} {"question" "q-353450" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-353450" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-79315" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The rate of growth of a car's displacement increases at a rate that's proportional to the time $t$ since the car started moving. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the car's displacement, $D,$ at time $t?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-79315" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The rate of growth of a **car's displacement** $D(t)$ **increases** at a **rate** that's **proportional** to the **time** $t$ since the car started moving.*\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *car's displacement* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *interval of time* since the car started moving. In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}∝t.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the car's displacement *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}=kt.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-79315" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b08e89e3902ba9360f9961f50e9f3f1b8ba1a959fe0de04a87724d72ff237043"} {"question" "q-79315" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-79315" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{D},\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{t},\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{kt}{D},\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}=kD,\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}=kt,\\,\\,k>0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-79315" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}=kt,\\,\\,k>0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-38593" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The number of weekly sales of a particular book decreases with time. The number of units sold at any given moment decreases at a rate that's proportional to the number of units sold at that moment. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the number of units sold $V(t)$ at time $t,$ where $t$ is the time since the book first went on sale?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-38593" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **number of units sold** at any given moment **decreases** at a **rate** that is **proportional** to **the number of units sold** at that moment.* \n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *number of units sold* of a particular book varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *number of units sold.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}∝V.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the number of units sold *decreases* with time, our derivative should be *negative*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=-kV.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-38593" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b08e89e3902ba9360f9961f50e9f3f1b8ba1a959fe0de04a87724d72ff237043"} {"question" "q-38593" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-38593" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=-kV,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=-tV"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=k+V,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=kV,\\,k>0"] ["math" "t\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=-V"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-38593" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=-kV,\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-38589" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Some people in a community contracted an unknown virus. The number of people infected by the virus increases at a rate that is proportional to the number of people infected by the virus. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the number of people who contracted the virus, $V,$ at time $t?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-38589" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **number of people** infected by the virus **increases** at a **rate** that is **proportional** to the **number of people** infected by the virus.* \n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *number of people* infected by the virus varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *number of people* infected. In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}∝V.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the number of people infected by the virus  *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=kV.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-38589" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b08e89e3902ba9360f9961f50e9f3f1b8ba1a959fe0de04a87724d72ff237043"} {"question" "q-38589" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-38589" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=k+V,\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=k-V,\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=kV,\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=tV"] ["math" "t\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=V"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-38589" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=kV,\\,\\,k>0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-38588" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The number of ants in an anthill increases at a rate that is proportional to the number of ants at the moment. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the number of ants, $A,$ at time $t?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-38588" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **number of ants** in an anthill **increases** at a **rate** that is **proportional** to the **number of ants** at the moment.* \n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *number of ants* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *number of ants.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}∝A.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the number of ants *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=kA.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-38588" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b08e89e3902ba9360f9961f50e9f3f1b8ba1a959fe0de04a87724d72ff237043"} {"question" "q-38588" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-38588" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=k+A,\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=k-A,\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=kA,\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=tA"] ["math" "t\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=A"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-38588" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=kA,\\,\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-38310" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the first year of a newborn's life, its height $H$ increases at a rate that is proportional to the time, in months, since birth.\nWhat differential equation describes the rate of change of the height of the baby at time $t?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-38310" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*For the first year of a newborn's life, its **height** $H$ **increases** at a **rate** that is **proportional** to the **time**, in months, since birth.*\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *height* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *time* since birth. In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}∝t.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the height *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=kt.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-38310" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b08e89e3902ba9360f9961f50e9f3f1b8ba1a959fe0de04a87724d72ff237043"} {"question" "q-38310" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-38310" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=-kH,\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=\\sqrt{kH},\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=kH,\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=k\\sqrt{t},\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=kt,\\,\\,k>0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-38310" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=kt,\\,\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-143029" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The population $P$ of mosquitos in a particular region increases with time. The rate of change of the population is proportional to the square of the population. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the population of mosquitos at time $t?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-143029" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **population** $P$ of mosquitos **increases** with time. The **rate** of change of the population of mosquitos is **proportional** to the **square of the population**.  *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *population* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *population squared.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}∝{P}^{2}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the population *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=k{P}^{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-143029" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b08e89e3902ba9360f9961f50e9f3f1b8ba1a959fe0de04a87724d72ff237043"} {"question" "q-143029" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-143029" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=-k\\sqrt{P},\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=-k{P}^{2},\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{{P}^{2}},\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=k\\sqrt{P},\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=k{P}^{2},\\,\\,k>0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-143029" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=k{P}^{2},\\,\\,k>0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-143036" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The velocity $v$ of a stone falling through some water to the bottom of a lake decreases with time. The rate of change of the stone's velocity is proportional to the square of the velocity. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the velocity at time $t?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-143036" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **velocity** $v$ of a stone falling through some water to the bottom of a lake **decreases** with time. The **rate** of change of the stone's velocity is **proportional** to the **square of the velocity**.  *\n\nWe note the following: \n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *velocity* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *velocity squared.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}∝{v}^{2}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the velocity *decreases* with time, our derivative should be *negative*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=-k{v}^{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-143036" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b08e89e3902ba9360f9961f50e9f3f1b8ba1a959fe0de04a87724d72ff237043"} {"question" "q-143036" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-143036" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{{v}^{2}},\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=-k{v}^{2},\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{{v}^{2}},\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=k\\sqrt{v},\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=k{v}^{2},\\,\\,k>0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-143036" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=-k{v}^{2},\\,\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-143037" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Construction waste stored in a large pile is taken to a landfill. The height $H$ of the pile decreases with time. The rate of change of the pile's height is proportional to the square of the height. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the height at time $t?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-143037" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **height** $H$ of the pile **decreases** with time. The **rate** of change of the pile's height is **proportional** to the **square of the height**.  *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *height* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *height squared.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}∝{H}^{2}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the height *decreases* with time, our derivative should be *negative*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=-k{H}^{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-143037" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b08e89e3902ba9360f9961f50e9f3f1b8ba1a959fe0de04a87724d72ff237043"} {"question" "q-143037" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-143037" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=-kH,\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=-k\\sqrt{H},\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=-k{H}^{2},\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{{H}^{2}},\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=k{H}^{2},\\,\\,k>0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-143037" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=-k{H}^{2},\\,\\,k>0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-51247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The value $V$ of a particular car decreases with time. The rate of change of the car's value is proportional to the square of the value. What differential equation describes the change of the value at time $t?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-51247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **value** $V$ of a particular car **decreases** with time. The **rate** of change of the car's value is **proportional** to the **value squared**.  *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *value* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *value squared.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}∝{V}^{2}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the value *decreases* with time, our derivative should be *negative*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=-k{V}^{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-51247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b08e89e3902ba9360f9961f50e9f3f1b8ba1a959fe0de04a87724d72ff237043"} {"question" "q-51247" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-51247" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=-kV,\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=-k\\sqrt{V},\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=-k{V}^{2},\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{{V}^{2}},\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=k{V}^{2},\\,\\,k>0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-51247" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=-k{V}^{2},\\,\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-143035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "During a certain chemical reaction, the volume of gas $G$ increases with time. The rate of change of the volume of gas is proportional to the square of the time $t,$ in seconds, since the reaction started. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the volume of gas at time $t?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-143035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*During a certain chemical reaction, the **volume** of gas $G$ **increases** with time. The **rate** of change of the volume of gas is **proportional** to the **square of the time** $t,$ in seconds.  *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *volume of gas* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}G}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}G}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *square of the time.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}G}{\\text{d}t}∝{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the volume of gas *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}G}{\\text{d}t}=k{t}^{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-143035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b08e89e3902ba9360f9961f50e9f3f1b8ba1a959fe0de04a87724d72ff237043"} {"question" "q-143035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-143035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}G}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{{t}^{2}},\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}G}{\\text{d}t}=-kt,\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}G}{\\text{d}t}=-k{t}^{2},\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}G}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{{t}^{2}},\\,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}G}{\\text{d}t}=k{t}^{2},\\,\\,k>0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-143035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}G}{\\text{d}t}=k{t}^{2},\\,\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-143058" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The height $H$ of a tree increases at a rate that's inversely proportional to the tree's height at that moment.\nWhat differential equation describes the rate of change of the height $H?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-143058" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **height** $H$ of a tree **increases** at a rate that's **inversely proportional** to the **tree's height** $H$ at that moment. *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *height* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}$ is *inversely proportional to* the *tree's height.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}∝\\frac{1}{H}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the height *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{H}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-143058" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b08e89e3902ba9360f9961f50e9f3f1b8ba1a959fe0de04a87724d72ff237043"} {"question" "q-143058" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-143058" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{H},\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=-kH,\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{H},\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{t},\\,k>0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=kH,\\,k>0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-143058" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}H}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{H},\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-143081" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The charge $C$ of a phone battery decreases at a rate that's inversely proportional to the time $t$ spent charging the smartphone. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the charge $C$ of the phone battery?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-143081" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **charge** $C$ of a phone battery **decreases** at a rate that's **inversely proportional** to the **time** $t$ spent charging the smartphone.*\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *charge* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}$ is *inversely proportional to* the *time.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}∝\\frac{1}{t}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the number *decreases* with time, our derivative should be *negative*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{t}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-143081" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b08e89e3902ba9360f9961f50e9f3f1b8ba1a959fe0de04a87724d72ff237043"} {"question" "q-143081" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037103/state.json" "file_sha256" "c5d7fce0fc900bfeddebcb41d2c55053505aab53f2373479582fcfe5d4590064"} {"question" "q-